#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# tutte_polynomial

#% text
# `tutte_polynomial(M, x, y)`: the Tutte polynomial of the matroid (or graphic matroid)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A matroid is `linear_matroid(A)` (the columns of a rational matrix), `graphic_matroid(edges)` (the edges of a graph), `uniform_matroid(r, m)` or `matroid(bases)` (bases as lists of elements 1, ..., m); its elements are numbered 1, ..., m, at most 22.

#% item
# T(1, 1) counts the bases (spanning trees of a connected graph) and T(2, 2) = 2^m.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
tutte_polynomial(graphic_matroid([[1, 2], [2, 3], [3, 1]]), x, y)
#% output
#= x + y + x^2

#% cell
tutte_polynomial(graphic_matroid(subsets([1, 2, 3, 4], [2])), x, y)
#% output
#= 2*x + 2*y + 3*x^2 + 3*y^2 + 4*x*y + x^3 + y^3

#% cell
tutte_polynomial(graphic_matroid(subsets([1, 2, 3, 4], [2])), 1, 1)
#% output
#= 16

#% cell
tutte_polynomial(uniform_matroid(2, 4), x, y)
#% output
#= 2*x + 2*y + x^2 + y^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `matroid_rank`, `matroid_bases`
